  "interpretation": "Actual unchanged upstream models and CPU sampler, not the earlier keyword heuristic. Scores are relative to the candidate pool, not probabilities or proof of novelty. Hosted proposals are generated ideas, not findings.",
  "release_catalog_check": {
    "catalog_sha256": "9675a6cf30af8cb572129e00511dab857d972cd116ab4b0c219aaaaf0323878f",
    "examples": [
      {
        "description_cluster": 121,
        "sample_text": "The 'genealogy of skills' framework tracks the transfer of knowledge by correlating improvements in specific internal capabilities (measured by narrow diagnostic probes) with overall performance gains on broad target benchmarks, revealing which intermediate training datasets effectively act as 'teachers' for required skills.",
        "matching_assignments": [
          {
            "assigned_cluster": -1,
            "paper_id": "conf__acl__PruksachatkunPL20"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "description_cluster": 121,
        "sample_text": "Initializing a small student model to functionally approximate a larger teacher model before fine-tuning\u2014rather than training from scratch\u2014improves knowledge transfer; this is achieved by first aligning the models' internal representations on unlabeled data and then using a dual-objective loss to match their output distributions.",
        "matching_assignments": [
          {
            "assigned_cluster": 166,
            "paper_id": "conf__acl__ChenSZCLW0024"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "description_cluster": 161,
        "sample_text": "Temperature Scaling reduces model overconfidence post-training by dividing raw output scores (logits) by a learnable parameter T before the final softmax layer; values of T greater than 1 'flatten' the probability distribution, lowering confidence scores without changing which class is predicted as the winner.",
        "matching_assignments": [
          {
            "assigned_cluster": 187,
            "paper_id": "conf__emnlp__JiangLD22"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "description_cluster": 161,
        "sample_text": "Advanced calibration techniques improve on simple linear scaling by using flexible mathematical frameworks\u2014such as Beta distributions or Gaussian Processes\u2014to model non-linear and non-monotonic relationships between a model\u2019s predicted confidence and its actual accuracy, allowing for more precise adjustments across the entire probability range.",
        "matching_assignments": [
          {
            "assigned_cluster": 158,
            "paper_id": "conf__emnlp__JiangLD22"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "description_cluster": 162,
        "sample_text": "Traditional Conformal Prediction relies on the assumption of exchangeability\u2014that future test data follows the same distribution as the calibration data\u2014meaning that when a model encounters 'uncertainty outliers' (samples significantly more complex or different than those seen during calibration), the statistical error guarantees become invalid and the model becomes miscalibrated.",
        "matching_assignments": [
          {
            "assigned_cluster": -1,
            "paper_id": "conf__acl__WangWZ00SX25"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "description_cluster": 162,
        "sample_text": "Selective Conformal Uncertainty (SConU) introduces a statistical 'significance test' for individual model predictions by calculating a conformal p-value that assesses whether a new input's predictive uncertainty is consistent with the distribution of uncertainty observed in a prior calibration set, allowing the system to refuse predictions for outliers that fall below a specific significance threshold.",
        "matching_assignments": [
          {
            "assigned_cluster": 138,
            "paper_id": "conf__acl__WangWZ00SX25"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
